Subject: [#94-6-175] State Schooling

I'd like to thank the fellow who posted stuff about the SATs - I'd do a 
better job of it, but netcom seems to have eaten my brilliantly-composed
reply :-).  I had been aware of the improvement in math scores, but they
still lag far behind those of other countries who spend less on schooling.

Most of the people I know who advocate reprivatizing schools would like to
do it with tuition vouchers or tax credits or a mixture thereof so that
poor people would be able to afford to pay for their kids to go to private
school, and so that other people wouldn't have to pay both for private
schooling and for State schooling.

I actually sort of like the US Tech Corps idea in a perverse sort of way.
I'm sure the State schooling partisans want to get advanced technology into
their classrooms to make it look like they're worth supporting, but the way
I see it is that letting kids get ahold of computer power, especially if
it's networked, will just help them figure out how little they have to learn
from State schoolteachers compared to the great big wide wonderful world out
there!

